&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;an&lt;strong&gt; Accounts Payable Manager&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the&lt;strong&gt; Controller, &lt;/strong&gt;to assist our expanding finance organization in &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach&lt;/strong&gt;. You will play a vital part in overseeing high-capacity invoice handling—with the department currently managing 4,000 monthly—while maintaining the precision of our Procure to Pay processes as we develop human-rated space stations.&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach&lt;/strong&gt; location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end accounts payable process, including invoice intake, two-way matching, three-way matching, GL coding, approval workflows, payment execution (ACH, domestic and international wire transfers, and checks), vendor reconciliations, and aging management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Process all payments with exceptional accuracy, verifying banking instructions, supporting documentation, approvals, and payment details to ensure error-free execution, particularly for international wire transfers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review invoices, purchase orders, contracts, and supporting documentation to identify discrepancies, ensure policy compliance, and maintain accurate financial records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the integrity of the accounts payable ledger through timely reconciliations, issue resolution, and support of month-end, quarter-end, and year-end close activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare audit-ready documentation and collaborate with external financial statement auditors to support efficient, accurate, and compliant audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Procurement/Supply Chain, Engineering, Program Management, and other departments to resolve discrepancies and ensure accurate and timely payment processing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and develop the accounts payable team while fostering a culture of accountability, accuracy, continuous improvement, and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate exceptional reliability through consistent attendance, responsiveness to time-sensitive payment requests, and availability during critical business periods, including weekends and evening hours to support&amp;nbsp; month-end close and audit activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of progressive accounts payable experience, including leadership or supervisory responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of GAAP, accounts payable best practices, and internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience processing domestic and international wire transfers with a high degree of accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting external financial statement audits and preparing audit-ready documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with ERP systems (e.g., NetSuite, SAP, Oracle, Microsoft Dynamics) and advanced Microsoft Excel skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail, organizational skills, analytical ability, and commitment to producing accurate, high-quality work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Skills: Proficiency in Netsuite and Ramp; intermediate Excel skills are strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background: Experience in the manufacturing or aerospace industry is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: Bachelor’s degree in Accounting or Business Administration strongly preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certifications: Certified Public Accountant&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work evenings and/or weekends to support critical mission milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work onsite in Long Beach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range: California&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$105,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$145,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;U.S. EXPORT CONTROL COMPLIANCE STATUS&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;The person hired will have access to information and items subject to U.S. export controls, and therefore, must either be a “U.S. person” as defined by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-22/section-120.62&quot;&gt;22 C.F.R. § 120.62&lt;/a&gt; or otherwise eligible for deemed export licensing. This status includes U.S. citizens, U.S. nationals, lawful permanent residents (green card holders), and asylees and refugees with such status granted, not pending.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EQUAL OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Vast is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with Vast is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for an &lt;strong&gt;Additive Manufacturing Technician&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the&lt;strong&gt; Supervisor, Manufacturing&lt;/strong&gt;, to support the development of the systems that will be required for the design and build of human-rated space stations. You will be responsible for the operation and maintenance of the additive manufacturing equipment, as well as part post-processing and quality control.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;non-exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach &lt;/strong&gt;location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Second Shift: 2pm - 10:30pm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setting up additive manufacturing print jobs, verifying machine settings against best practices, overseeing the print process and quality as the machine operates, recover build pauses if necessary&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safely handling the metal powder before and after the build, includes sieving, loading, part de-powdering, measuring, and safe storage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep a clean, organized, and thoroughly maintained work space&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and implement process efficiency improvement projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently perform verifications and document results in a clear, precise, and complete manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate post processing equipment such as drills, handheld grinders and CNC machines as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform preventive routine maintenance on the machines and troubleshooting manufacturing hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support rapid iteration and development testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document build, test, and maintenance activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adhere to and help refine test processes, safety standards, and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support other teams through cross-functional collaboration and training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school degree or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of manufacturing, or similar industry, experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working with hand tools, basic measurement equipment, and following detailed procedures exactly and safely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years experience in additive manufacturing or similar environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read, interpret and work from drawings, controlled documentation and processes such as: assembly procedures/work instructions, schematics, engineering drawings, and parts list&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in aerospace or defense manufacturing environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience driving engagement with others, taking initiative, and helping push the team to new levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with metal powders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work overtime, or weekends to support critical mission milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 50 lbs unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range: California&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$23&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$58 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;U.S. EXPORT CONTROL COMPLIANCE STATUS&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;The person hired will have access to information and items subject to U.S. export controls, and therefore, must either be a “U.S. person” as defined by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-22/section-120.62&quot;&gt;22 C.F.R. § 120.62&lt;/a&gt; or otherwise eligible for deemed export licensing. This status includes U.S. citizens, U.S. nationals, lawful permanent residents (green card holders), and asylees and refugees with such status granted, not pending.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EQUAL OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Vast is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with Vast is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for an &lt;strong&gt;Associate Creative Director, Brand &amp;amp; Design&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the&lt;strong&gt; Senior Director, Brand Design, &lt;/strong&gt;to help build and protect the creative standard for how Vast shows up in the world&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt; You&#39;ll be in the work every day: designing, art directing, and solving creative problems directly, while giving clear direction to a small team and mentoring the people on it. You help shape the creative direction for key brand moments, then roll up your sleeves to make the work great.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Long Beach &lt;/strong&gt;location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and evolve Vast&#39;s brand design standards, and make sure the work coming out of the team meets them every day, not just at major launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage a team of designers day-to-day: give feedback in real time, run reviews, and set clear direction on what good looks like&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Jump into the work yourself, sketching, editing, designing, when that&#39;s the fastest way to get something over the bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead creative work from concept through final execution across brand initiatives, campaigns, and key company moments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business goals and technical complexity into creative direction the team can actually run with&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with marketing, comms, product, engineering, and business teams to spot where design can move the needle, and follow through on it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor designers on craft and judgment, not just process, help them get better at knowing what to cut&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present creative direction to stakeholders, and hold the line on quality when there&#39;s pressure to compromise&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep a real pulse on how AI is changing design and production workflows, and bring that into how the team actually works&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in brand, design, art direction, or a related creative discipline (e.g., brand design, digital design, visual communications, integrated marketing), with a proven track record of producing high-quality work yourself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong portfolio that demonstrates hands-on craft across multiple channels and audiences, with a clear pull toward innovative, simple, and technically-minded work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fast-paced environment, and genuinely enjoying the pace, volume, and ambiguity that come with it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing a small design team: giving clear creative direction while staying deeply hands-on in the work itself&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A natural people mentor who develops direct reports and helps them grow their craft and confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating business objectives, audience insights, and complex concepts into clear, executable creative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with cross-functional teams including marketing, communications, product, engineering, operations, and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building brand in aerospace, technology, science, or another category where the product is genuinely hard to explain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable across brand design standards, design for print, ads, social, events, partnerships, mission graphics, facilities and wayfinding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating highly technical, hard-to-explain products into stories that land with a broader audience without losing credibility with a technical one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing external creative partners and production resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in the room with engineers and executives, able to hold a point of view under pressure and get people aligned without watering down the work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 10% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work overtime, or weekends to support critical mission milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range: California&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$151,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$256,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;U.S. EXPORT CONTROL COMPLIANCE STATUS&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;The person hired will have access to information and items subject to U.S. export controls, and therefore, must either be a “U.S. person” as defined by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-22/section-120.62&quot;&gt;22 C.F.R. § 120.62&lt;/a&gt; or otherwise eligible for deemed export licensing. This status includes U.S. citizens, U.S. nationals, lawful permanent residents (green card holders), and asylees and refugees with such status granted, not pending.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EQUAL OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Vast is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with Vast is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for an&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Avionics Design Reliability Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Director of Design Reliability&lt;/strong&gt;, to guide the design, verification, and validation of Haven-1, the world&#39;s first commercial human-rated space station.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Avionics Design Reliability Engineer, you will ensure avionics, RF, and power systems on Haven-1 are appropriately designed and function reliably, without failure, over their intended lifespan by integrating reliability principles directly into the design process. You will drive Failure Modes and Effects Analysis (FMEA), guide test plan definition and review verification &amp;amp; validation data, and facilitate design teams to prevent failures before manufacturing. You will work closely with hardware teams to ensure build practices meet design intent, define test methodologies, and analyze field data to improve design robustness. You will be responsible for shepherding the Haven-1 avionics, RF, and power systems through detailed design and transitioning the space station from design,&amp;nbsp; to a built and tested station ready to host humans in space.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach&lt;/strong&gt; location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical Leadership:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide design of avionics, RF, and power systems on a large scale space station.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate Vast&#39;s understanding of electrical, RF, and power system analysis considerations to drive design decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical reviews providing clear, decisive guidance of mechanical design and analysis, manufacturing drawings, test plans, concept of operations, during milestone design reviews and major risk gates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide critical peer review and approval of hardware designs during design reviews, and of acceptance and qualification test campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that the Vasts design process &amp;amp; design criteria/requirements are being followed for flight, launch, and ground support systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the standard for acceptance and qualification test completeness for flight systems, ensuring our test campaigns are robust, disciplined, and aligned with human-rated reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring deep engineering intuition to test campaigns, identifying risks early and helping teams converge on safe, resilient solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design Excellence:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect Vast’s avionics, RF, power, and EMI/EMC engineering standards, design guides, and review frameworks; build tools that enable fast, confident decision-making at all levels across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop design criteria, requirements, and verification approaches to support haven-1 design architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make engineering best practices accessible and actionable, especially for engineers moving rapidly under ambitious program timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and elevate engineering teams across the organization by bringing broad experience in design, build cycles, integration, and test.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn organizational knowledge into lasting guidance by capturing lessons learned and strengthening future standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Ownership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and steward the processes that ensure engineering rigor at scale—ensuring designs meet standards, reviews are comprehensive, and changes are consistently implemented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously refine design review templates, reliability checklists, and internal design guides.&lt;/li&gt;
