&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Director, Lunar Programs&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Chief Policy Officer &lt;/strong&gt;to lead all NASA-focused business development for Vast&#39;s lunar and cislunar initiatives. This role will lead customer engagement, opportunity development, capture strategy, and partnership efforts that advance Vast&#39;s initiatives to operate the world&#39;s leading in-space infrastructure in support of NASA&#39;s lunar exploration objectives, including&amp;nbsp; a sustained human presence at the Moon.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time, exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach, CA, Houston, TX or Washington, D.C.&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute a comprehensive NASA lunar market strategy aligned with Vast&#39;s revenue and mission objectives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Leadership, Engineering, Policy and Government Relations, Marketing, Legal, Communications, and other internal teams to ensure alignment between NASA lunar customer needs and station and lunar system development priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate the preparation and delivery of lunar briefings to support strategic planning and NASA engagement activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead internal planning for NASA lunar opportunity prioritization, capture strategy, and pipeline development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead customer engagement across opportunity identification, mission scoping, capability briefings, and early concept development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, shape, and advance opportunities for NASA use of Vast systems across crewed lunar missions, cislunar operations, experimentation, and training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze NASA budget requests, congressional appropriations, and authorization language to anticipate shifts in lunar program funding and priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise Vast leadership on programmatic considerations such as&amp;nbsp; cost, schedule, and risk posture that shape the viability and structure of NASA lunar opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships with NASA&#39;s international partners and their industry teams (e.g., ESA, JAXA, CSA, MBRSC) to identify multilateral opportunities and partnership constructs supporting sustained lunar presence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop business cases, pricing strategy inputs, and ROM cost estimates in coordination with finance and program management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support proposal development and coordinate cross functional contributions from engineering, program management, legal, and operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Vast at space industry events where civil space and government stakeholders are present&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver presentations, participate in panels, and provide senior-level briefings that communicate the capabilities and value of Vast lunar systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in engineering, physics, aerospace, business, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of relevant experience including substantial work in agency business development, capture management, civil space programs, or government contracting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of procurement and contract structures, including IDIQ, OTA, FFP, CPFF, Space Act Agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication, analytical, collaboration, and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical understanding and ability to communicate complex systems to agency and civil space audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate independently, prioritize effectively, and manage multiple efforts simultaneously in a fast paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master&#39;s degree in engineering, science, business, or a space policy discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with NASA Headquarters, Johnson Space Center, Marshall Space Flight Center, Kennedy Space Center, the Artemis program, or similar organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the flexible acquisition and partnership approaches NASA uses to explore new technologies, support research and experimentation, and rapidly evaluate emerging commercial capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience leading efforts that secured major programs or awards, including strategy, teaming, and proposal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with sensitive or controlled program information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 30% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to obtain and maintain any required government clearances&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range: California&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$194,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$275,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
