&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for an &lt;strong&gt;Integration Engineer, Launch Operations&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Senior Integration Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, to support vehicle-level integration, launch processing, and launch campaign execution for our&amp;nbsp; human-rated space stations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time, exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach&lt;/strong&gt; location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and manage vehicle configuration states for test readiness, shipping, and launch processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute ATLO sequences for Haven-1, coordinating vehicle state transitions between integration, test, and launch operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop planning for critical handling of flight hardware and MGSE (lifting, weighing, breakover, transport)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support launch site operations including payload processing, vehicle stacking, and launch campaign execution at Cape Canaveral and/or other launch facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with integration test, tooling, and other stakeholder teams to determine tooling requirements, address vehicle access constraints, and ensure vehicle safety prior to launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure vehicle meets cleanliness, contamination control, and environmental requirements during all stages of integration, transport, and launch processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author integration planning, issue work orders, and work directly with production and technicians to execute work on the vehicle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other engineers, subject matter experts, and technicians to solve complex integration issues in real time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support system checkouts, functional testing, and vehicle health verification during launch campaign windows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with launch provider and range personnel to ensure compliance with payload processing facility requirements and range safety procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor of Science degree in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or related engineering discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of aerospace integration engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Direct experience supporting spacecraft launch campaigns, including payload processing, system checkouts, and/or launch site operations (e.g., Cape Canaveral, Vandenberg, KSC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with spacecraft hardware integration, including critical lifts, transport, and mechanical/electrical mate operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working alongside technicians and directing multi-person integration operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience authoring integration procedures, work orders, and sequencing plans for vehicle-level operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of aerospace integration engineering experience with progressive ownership of ATLO or vehicle-level integration through launch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as the responsible engineer or integration lead for end-to-end launch campaign execution, including driving requirements and building processes from scratch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payload processing facilities, range safety procedures, and contamination control requirements (cleanroom protocols, Class 100K or better)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with vehicle-level functional testing, health checks, TCS, and/or propulsion fill operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining vehicle configuration states for test readiness, shipping, and launch processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NX or similar mechanical design tools for MGSE and fixture design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills for coordinating across engineering, technicians, vendors, and range/launch provider personnel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with spacecraft critical lifts, breakovers, and mass property measurements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 10% during nominal operations. During active launch campaign windows (estimated 1–2 months per campaign), travel may increase to 50%+ including extended deployment to Cape Canaveral or other launch facilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work overtime, off-hours/shift schedules, and weekends to support critical mission milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 25 lbs unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
