&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Lead Integration Build Engineer,&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp; reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Manager, Integration&lt;/strong&gt;, to support the development of the systems required for the&amp;nbsp; build and test of artificial-gravity human-rated space stations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a lead for the Integration Build Engineering team, you will develop creative solutions to complex assembly, integration, and test problems. You will play a critical role in our development and production teams for identifying and defining human-rated vehicle processes, and growing a team that exists at the center of Haven-1 execution. Your input will be vital in transitioning the space station from design to a built and tested station ready to host humans in space.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;exempt &lt;/strong&gt;position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach &lt;/strong&gt;location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and grow a team of engineers and specialists charged with developing, scaling, and maintaining the facilities, tooling, and processes used to build, test, and integrate flight hardware for Haven-1&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support day-to-day execution of hardware production and vehicle-level integration, ensuring builds are safe, on schedule, cost-effective, and produce hardware that performs on orbit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate as an interdisciplinary engineer that can&amp;nbsp; collect production requirements, then plan and execute the build, integration, and validation of flight hardware against those requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement tooling and fixture solutions that are required for all phases of Haven-1’s integration campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge existing design and process requirements, remove unnecessary steps, and optimize the build for a highly reliable vehicle that can meet schedule demands&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become a subject-matter expert for the build of&amp;nbsp; vehicle-level systems (e.g., structures, propulsion, thermal, ECLSS, or avionics), maintaining working knowledge of its design, schematics, and requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate nonconformances, identify root causes and robust solutions, and drive corrective actions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate and maintain design-for-manufacturing requirements and work instructions/test procedures used to build flight hardware&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear goals for the team and hold members accountable for execution and continuous improvement in their area of ownership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the relationship with design engineering, supply chain, mission management, and other cross-functional partner teams&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities for team growth and develop training to increase overall engineering effectiveness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in mechanical, manufacturing, aerospace, electrical, or similar field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of related engineering experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the build, assembly, integration, or test of complex assemblies and systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on hardware manufacturing, integration, or test experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with working with technicians and running multi person operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing procedures, technical presentations, and providing go/no-go judgment and rationale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years of experience leading teams, projects, or people&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Epsilon3 and Python environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to make independent judgments with limited information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience planning and executing vehicle level system verifications, leak checks, or environmental tests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a high-stress environment balancing several projects at any given time, and the flexibility to adjust for abrupt changes in strategic direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GD&amp;amp;T and complex tolerance stack-ups&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mechanical design and analysis; familiarity with Siemens NX/Teamcenter or similar PLM tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing work instructions, test plans, and procedures, and configuration management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of PFMEA and&amp;nbsp; Root Cause/Corrective Action, and equivalent quality-oriented problem solving approaches&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong sense of ownership, drive, and effective communication&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable making highly impactful decisions in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 25% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work overtime, or weekends to support critical mission milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 25lbs unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range: California&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$120,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$194,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
