&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Receiving Quality Inspector, Avionics&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to &lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, Quality&lt;/strong&gt;, to support the development of the systems that will be required for the design and build of human-rated space stations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;non-exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach &lt;/strong&gt;location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performs dimensional, visual, and workmanship inspections of avionics hardware, including printed circuit boards (PCBs), electronic components, and wire harnesses using established procedures with minimum supervision of a higher inspector or supervisor&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review all supplied documentation for hardware acceptance per engineering requirements and document, track, and complete discrepancy reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform review of first articles and conduct receiving inspections of avionics hardware and electronic components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect PCBs for workmanship, component identification, orientation, solder quality, damage, contamination, and other defects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify electronic components against engineering drawings, bills of material, purchase orders, part numbers, revisions, manufacturer information, and applicable specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect soldering, crimping, conformal coating, staking, surface mounted devices, and through-hole components in accordance with applicable NASA and IPC workmanship standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform detailed inspections of wire harnesses, connectors, terminals, splices, shielding, labeling, and other associated hardware&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide feedback to engineers, buyers, and suppliers with inspection data and identified discrepancies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform basic electrical testing and verification using portable measuring devices and established test equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate and perform Verification activities on Non-Conforming Material Reports&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 3 years of experience in equal or related field in receiving or Avionics inspection of aerospace components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read, interpret, and work to blueprints, drawings, and process and design specifications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience doing First Article Inspections and Source Inspections&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience inspecting solder, crimping, conformal coating, staking, and surface mounted devices in accordance with NASA 8739 and/or IPC-J-STD-001, IPC-A-610 standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wire harness experience in accordance with NASA-STD-8739.3 and 8739.4 and/or IPC-A-620 standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with performing electronic testing and inspection using portable measuring devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform detailed in-process and final inspections on complex flight hardware, including PCB assemblies, custom harnesses, rack/panel assemblies, and integrated systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High School or equivalent diploma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be dedicated to the quality function and possess a drive to enhance the quality of both the product and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have computer skills including the use of MS Suite and an ability to be comfortable using ERP / MRP applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with ESD-sensitive components and ESD-controlled environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using microscopes or other magnification equipment for detailed PCB and electronic assembly inspection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience interpreting electrical schematics, PCB drawings, assembly drawings, and bills of material&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with component traceability, date/lot codes, manufacturer part numbers, and Certificates of Conformance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivation and ability to prioritize projects to meet completion dates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to make independent judgments with limited information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication skills for relaying data (verbally and in-writing) between other employees, vendors, and customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a high-stress environment balancing several projects at any given time, and the flexibility to adjust for abrupt changes in strategic direction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work evenings and/or weekends to support critical mission milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Physical requirements include frequent and repetitive use of hands; ability to push, pull or lift up to 35 pounds; vision acuity 20/25 (with or without corrective lenses)&lt;/li&gt;
