&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Buyer&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the&lt;strong&gt; E-2 Manager of Supply Chain, &lt;/strong&gt;to create the world&#39;s highest performing engine for small launchers, while optimizing for production and low cost. In this role, you will join a team with exciting momentum that has produced and successfully tested fully integrated engine development samples. You will be a key member who will help transition the system from development to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a full-time,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Hawthorne&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build up a strategic supply chain supporting engine components including off-the-shelf components, tools, material, avionics components and any hardware assemblies are associated with it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand BOM cost and run should-cost analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and take part in meetings with engineering to develop a strong rapport&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with manufacturing and engineering teams to identify and execute cost savings opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alleviate any delivery blockages including supply, quality or invoice disputes Identify areas for improvement and develop new processes or KPI’s to further team development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a mentor for the team and provide trainings on the commodity to cross-train team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a good understanding of global markets and economics and its effect on Aerospace Supply Chains Issue RFQ’s, PO’s within a timely manner and maintain established service levels for quotes, purchase orders and updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to balance multiple priorities with ambiguous instructions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4 years in a procurement function, 2 years in aerospace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 years in a position requiring traceability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 years working with an ERP system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor of Science degree in Supply Chain, Business or Engineering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
