&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Partnerships Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team. Reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;VP, Communications and dotted line to the Head of Partnerships,&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;you are a commercially minded, highly organized marketing and communications professional who will own the day-to-day management of Vast’s existing brand partnerships and work closely with the Head of Brand Partnerships to develop and build new partnership opportunities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have experience developing and managing brand partnerships, and a strong understanding of the media and communications landscape. We would love someone who brings creativity and cultural fluency to the role: this is a rare opportunity to shape how brands and consumers engage with the future of space exploration.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time, exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach &lt;/strong&gt;location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the day-to-day management of Vast’s existing brand partnerships, serving as the primary point of contact and relationship manager&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead delivery against contractual commitments, tracking deliverables, activation timelines and campaign performance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and develop opportunities to expand existing partnerships in alignment with partner objectives and new opportunities in Vast’s ecosystem&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and identify prospective brand partners that align with Vast’s mission&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a well-organized pipeline, tracking outreach, prospect status, deal stages and actions and provide regular reporting to the VP, Communications/ Head of Brand Partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Head of Brand Partnerships and Marketing &amp;amp; Design colleagues to develop creative concepts, presentation materials, and pitch decks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ideal candidate will also support the Communications team from time-to-time as needed. This could include managing announcements, media engagements and public engagement campaigns, reviewing press materials and developing and aligning communications plans across partner agencies and Vast.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
