&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Photo Editor&lt;/strong&gt; to join its Media Production team on a fixed-term basis, reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, Media Production&lt;/strong&gt;. The ideal candidate is a technically precise, visually confident retoucher who can move fast without cutting corners, and who understands color and light well enough to make judgment calls, not just execute a brief. This is a high-leverage engagement: the work this person does in a short window will directly determine how consistent and premium Vast&#39;s photography looks going forward.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on, IC role for someone who can walk into an existing body of work, understand the visual direction, and both execute against it and help define it more clearly. You&#39;ll work through a real backlog of unedited production photography, and in parallel help formalize the color, light, and retouching standards the team uses so decisions don&#39;t have to be re-made from scratch on every shoot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an in-person role based in &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach, CA&lt;/strong&gt; and runs as a &lt;strong&gt;60 day fixed-term position&lt;/strong&gt;, with potential to extend.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear the Backlog: Process existing unedited photography from past shoots to final, delivery-ready quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Post-Production &amp;amp; Workflow: Manage file handling from ingest to delivery (filenaming, packaging, archiving) and build reusable presets to streamline operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define Visual Standards: Partner with the Media Production team to document and maintain consistent color, light, and retouching standards across all photography and photographers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Live Production (as needed): Oversee capture-to-delivery for active shoots, including providing on-set Digitech support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Photography (as needed): Execute product, hardware, portrait, or event photography as required, maintaining the same high quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
