&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior RF Systems Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the&lt;strong&gt; Director, RF Engineering,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;to support the development of the systems that will be required for the design and build of artificial-gravity human-rated space stations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Long Beach&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support system level design and modeling of spacecraft communications systems including space to Earth, space to space, and crew audio &amp;amp; multimedia links.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate requirements, concepts of operations, block diagrams, and high level analysis for artificial gravity space stations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with integration and operations teams to define checkout procedures, LEOP, orbital phase, docking, crewed operations, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with a multidisciplinary engineering team to form tightly integrated avionics, structures, thermal control, and software systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in electrical engineering or related engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of experience in an RF engineering role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RF test equipment such as Spectrum Analyzers, VNAs, Power Meters, Cable Analyzers, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in software development: Matlab, Python, C/C++, or other programming languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with RF communication system design &amp;amp; analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MS or PhD in&amp;nbsp; ECE, EE, Physics, or related stem discipline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with RF analysis software: HFSS, STK, ADS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of in space effects including ionizing radiation, atomic oxygen, plasma charging, MMOD, outgassing, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work in spacecraft system design and/or operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of RF modulation and media access control schemes such as BPSK, SOQPSK, GMSK, APSK, TDMA, FDMA, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of communication system coding and error correction schemes such as Reed Solomon, LDPC, BCH, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with common space communications interoperability standards such as CCSDS and DVB-S2&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Ethernet and IP networking, VPNs, TCP, UDP, L2/L3 switches, VLANs, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with serial communication protocols such as CAN, SPI, and I2C, RS-422/485&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
