&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior / Staff Build Reliability Engineer (Avionics),&lt;/strong&gt; reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Director of Build &amp;amp; Supplier Reliability&lt;/strong&gt;, to support the reliability of flight avionics hardware across the product lifecycle for our human-rated space stations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Long Beach&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Build Reliability for avionics hardware and work centers, setting expectations for reliability, manufacturability, and build and flight readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Manufacturing, Quality, Supply Chain, and Mission Assurance leadership to ensure robust, scalable quality and verification plans across the product lifecycle, with lessons consistently carried across programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure successful introduction of flight hardware by defining readiness criteria–including process qualification, manufacturability, and inspectability–and driving the retirement of build risks through production ramp-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive maturation of internal avionics production processes, ensuring documentation, equipment, tooling, process controls, data collection, and training support consistent and streamlined execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure off-nominal work is performed and documented reliably. Partner with Mission Assurance to drive risk mitigations and steer response plans to severe issues. Provide leadership and technical direction for high-visibility issues, establishing recovery plans and aligning operations, quality, and engineering on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect and analyze build data to identify risk and recurring issues. Lead build quality reviews, generate data-driven recommendations, and effectively influence partner teams to prioritize efforts that prevent escapes and improve reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead containment and root-cause investigation of high-impact Avionics-related issues. Ensure implementation and verification of robust corrective actions that address root cause and systemic contributors across Vast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead major cost reduction initiatives through simplification of requirements, clearer design standards, streamlined inspection and process validation steps, and strengthened process controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor individuals and teams to elevate reliability capabilities across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in an engineering discipline or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in quality, manufacturing, reliability, or design in aerospace, defense, or high-reliability hardware environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional initiatives with executive visibility and influence technical direction across organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and technical leadership skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
