&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior / Staff Build Reliability Engineer (Integration),&lt;/strong&gt; reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Director of Build &amp;amp; Supplier Reliability&lt;/strong&gt;, to support the reliability of vehicle integration and test operations across the product lifecycle for our human-rated space stations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;exempt &lt;/strong&gt;position located in our&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Long Beach&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Build Reliability for vehicle integration and test work centers, setting expectations for reliability, manufacturability, and build and flight readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Engineering, Manufacturing, Quality, Supply Chain, and Mission Assurance leadership to ensure robust, scalable quality and verification plans across the product lifecycle, with lessons consistently carried across programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure successful introduction of flight hardware by defining integration readiness criteria–including process qualification, design for manufacturability and assembly, and inspectability–and driving the retirement of risks through production ramp-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive maturation of integration and test processes, ensuring documentation, equipment, tooling, process controls, data collection, and training support consistent and streamlined execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure off-nominal work is performed and documented reliably. Partner with Mission Assurance to drive risk mitigations and steer response plans to severe issues. Provide leadership and technical direction for high-visibility issues, establishing recovery plans and aligning operations, quality, and engineering on execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collect and analyze build data to identify risk and recurring issues. Lead build quality reviews, generate data-driven recommendations, and effectively influence upstream and partner teams to prioritize efforts that prevent escapes and improve vehicle reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead containment and root-cause investigation of high-impact vehicle issues. Ensure implementation and verification of robust corrective actions that address root cause and systemic contributors across Vast.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead major cost reduction initiatives through simplification of requirements, clearer design and integration standards, streamlined inspection and process validation steps, and strengthened&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;process controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor individuals and teams to elevate reliability capabilities across the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in an engineering discipline or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in quality, manufacturing, reliability, or design in aerospace, defense, or high-reliability hardware environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead cross-functional initiatives with executive visibility and influence technical direction across organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and technical leadership skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of driving systemic improvements and shaping engineering strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in reliability engineering, quality systems, and standards (ISO 9001, AS9100, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mastery of advanced reliability and quality tools (RCA, FMEA, SPC, control plans); Six Sigma Black Belt or equivalent experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical depth in hardware integration, assembly operations, and/or test operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 10%.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to support mission-critical events outside normal working hours.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pay Range:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior Build Reliability Engineer: $137,760 - $162,960 - $195,552&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Staff Build Reliability Engineer: $162,360 - $192,060 - $230,472&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range: California&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$137,760&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$230,472 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
