&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EQUAL OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Vast is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with Vast is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Welder - 2nd Shift &lt;/strong&gt;reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Shop Floor Supervisor - 2nd Shift, &lt;/strong&gt;to support the development of the systems that will be required for the design and build of artificial-gravity human-rated space stations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a &lt;strong&gt;full-time&lt;/strong&gt;,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;non-exempt &lt;/strong&gt;position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2nd Shift Hours: 2:00 PM to 10:30 PM&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Weld the Haven Structure for Human spaceflight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate mechanized and robotic welding equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to quickly fabricate, weld tooling to support Haven.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect fabricated parts for geometry acceptance and weld conformance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fit, form parts, and clean parts as required and setup welding equipment in preparation for welding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform Class A quality Aluminum weld&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose weld defects and suggest corrective actions, both in repair and process optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Engineering to improve tools and problem solve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Material handling of raw goods and finished weldments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a wide variety of metal fabrication equipment such as vertical bandsaw, Sanding equipment, Capability to efficiently set up jig tables&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with Class A TIG&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience with fabrication, and forming experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience reading engineering blueprints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to follow written and verbal instruction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar working with x-ray technicians and other NDT techniques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automated/robotic welding experience Preferred VPPAW&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter, highly motivated working in a fast-paced department&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ or more years with Class A aerospace welding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel up to 10% of the time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work evenings and/or weekends to support critical mission milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 50 lbs unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range: California&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$45.10&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$64.02 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;U.S. EXPORT CONTROL COMPLIANCE STATUS&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;The person hired will have access to information and items subject to U.S. export controls, and therefore, must either be a “U.S. person” as defined by&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-22/section-120.62&quot;&gt;22 C.F.R. § 120.62&lt;/a&gt; or otherwise eligible for deemed export licensing. This status includes U.S. citizens, U.S. nationals, lawful permanent residents (green card holders), and asylees and refugees with such status granted, not pending.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EQUAL OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Vast is an Equal Opportunity Employer; employment with Vast is governed on the basis of merit, competence and qualifications and will not be influenced in any manner by race, color, religion, gender, national origin/ethnicity, veteran status, disability status, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, mental or physical disability or any other legally protected status.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;SMT Test Technician &lt;/strong&gt;reporting to the Supervisor, Structures Test, assisting in development, qualification, and acceptance testing for the Haven-1 components and structure.&amp;nbsp; This role is for a hands-on person with great attention to detail and excellent people skills.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a full-time,&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;non-exempt &lt;/strong&gt;position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach&lt;/strong&gt; location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assists engineering with projects and test campaigns with instrumentation and DAQ support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can setup and operate tests with engineering guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently brings improvements to engineering with a plan to implement them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setup structural and mechanisms tests for development, qualification, and acceptance test campaigns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow engineering drawings and schematics to execute test procedures/plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of fabrication skills (welding, machining, sheet metal, drilling, mill and lathe)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare test set-ups that may involve crane operations and assist in lifting operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work on problems of diverse or complex scope with minimal to no guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make independent decisions and take action within established practices and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in updating test procedures and provide feedback to improve robustness/automation/duration&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoots DAQ and/or test setup issues and implements solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist engineering with test fixture design and implement best practices for DFM/T (Design for Manufacturability/Test)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review test requirements, RFQs (Request for Quote), SOWs (Statement of Work), etc. as it relates to testing and test equipment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of running data logging and data processing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has extensive knowledge of a variety of instrumentation (to include load cells, pressure transducers, strain gages, thermocouples, deflection transducers) and can recommend what should be used during testing to fulfil requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can independently create and execute tasks/projects autonomously&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Can find issues and implement solutions before they happen&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assists with training and mentoring less experienced team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Has prior experience in a specific testing field and electrical experience combined (3+years)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;HS Diploma or equivalency certificate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of running tests using manufacturing and operational procedure focused software&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting up hydraulic load and structures testing for aerospace components/vehicles, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting up leak and pneumatic pressure testing for aerospace components and vehicles, or similar&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient knowledge and skill working with various sensors (strain gauges, load cells, pressure transducers, thermocouples, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of PMS (Preventative Maintenance Schedule) of testing equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of data acquisition systems (Analog inputs, analog output, digital inputs, digital outputs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with relevant aerospace testing standards (SMC-S-016, MIL-STD-810G, GSFC-STD-7000B, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Jira project management and Google apps: gmail, docs, sheets, slides, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of maintaining calibrations of instrumentation devices (load cells, pressure transducers, power supplies, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of test equipment assembly and fabrication: hydraulic hoses, AN fittings with stainless steel hardline, unistrut, 80/20, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work overtime, or weekends to support critical mission milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 25 lbs unassisted&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel to Mojave Air and Space Port with short notice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to to work from elevated heights and outdoor environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range: California&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$29.37&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$56.92 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
