&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Supervisor of Avionics Manufacturing - Electro Mechanical&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to &lt;strong&gt;Manager of Avionics Manufacturing, &lt;/strong&gt;to support the development of the systems that will be required for the design and build of artificial-gravity human-rated space stations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a full-time, &lt;strong&gt;exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located in our &lt;strong&gt;Long Beach&lt;/strong&gt; location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shift hours:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Second shift: 2:00PM - 10:30PM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize, coordinate, prioritize, and communicate day-to-day electro-mechanical and electronics assembly work assignments for the second shift technician team, ensuring smooth and productive continuity from first shift operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, mentor, and model a strong work ethic, safety culture, and quality-first mindset on the production floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train and onboard new team members in electronics assembly techniques, soldering workmanship standards, and IPC J-STD-001 requirements, ensuring all personnel meet and maintain applicable soldering certification expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support technicians in daily tasks including through-hole and surface mount soldering, component placement, PCB assembly, electro-mechanical integration, wire termination, connector assembly, and conformal coating in accordance with IPC J-STD-001 acceptance criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with optimizing the electronics and electro-mechanical manufacturing process, considering factors such as cycle time, yield, quality, and cost-effectiveness while maintaining compliance with IPC J-STD-001 Class 2 and Class 3 standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design reviews, providing practical manufacturing insight to improve the solderability, assemblability, and reliability of electronic and electro-mechanical assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with quality assurance teams to establish, maintain, and enforce rigorous quality control processes aligned with IPC J-STD-001 workmanship standards, including in-process inspections, solder joint evaluations, and final acceptance testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives by identifying opportunities to reduce soldering defects, minimize rework, eliminate waste, and improve overall electronics assembly quality and throughput.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet demanding second shift production schedules to achieve high output rates while maintaining IPC J-STD-001 compliance and adapting to shifting priorities in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clean, organized, and well-stocked production area, including ESD controls, tool control, consumable inventory (solder, flux, cleaning agents, conformal coating materials, etc.), and support of build infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Read and interpret technical drawings, schematics, assembly drawings, Bills of Materials (BOMs), and work instructions to support assembly and inspection activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 5 years of professional experience in a technical field, with a strong preference for candidates with a background in electronics or electro-mechanical assembly manufacturing, preferably within the aerospace or defense industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in a leadership or supervisory role, with demonstrated ability to guide, motivate, and manage production teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High School Diploma or equivalency certificate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth understanding of electronics and electro-mechanical manufacturing processes including SMT (Surface Mount Technology), through-hole soldering, hand soldering, rework and repair, conformal coating, potting, electro-mechanical integration, and functional/electrical testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IPC J-STD-001 CIS or CIT certification, with the ability to train, evaluate, and certify technicians to IPC soldering workmanship standards.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of and experience operating within a formal quality management system such as AS9100, ISO 9001, or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid working knowledge of IPC J-STD-001 soldering standards; IPC J-STD-001 CIS (Certified IPC Specialist) or CIT (Certified IPC Trainer) certification is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with complementary IPC standards including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IPC-A-610 (Acceptability of Electronic Assemblies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IPC-7711/7721 (Rework, Modification, and Repair of Electronic Assemblies)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;IPC-HDBK-001 (J-STD-001 Supporting Handbook)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;J-STD-004/005/006 (Requirements for Flux, Solder Paste, and Solder Alloys)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with ESD (Electrostatic Discharge) control practices and compliance with ANSI/ESD S20.20 standards in an electronics manufacturing environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating and maintaining manufacturing documentation such as Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs), Work Instructions, Routers, and Inspection Criteria aligned with IPC J-STD-001.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CAD or EDA tools (such as Altium, Siemens NX, or similar) for reviewing electronic assembly drawings, schematics, and BOMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving skills and the ability to perform structured root cause analysis (RCA) and implement effective corrective actions for soldering and assembly defects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with functional testing, electrical testing, and troubleshooting of electronic and electro-mechanical assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of lean manufacturing principles and process improvement methodologies (Six Sigma, 5S, Kaizen) as applied to electronics manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and cross-functional collaboration skills, with the ability to interface effectively with engineering, quality, and program management teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and an unwavering commitment to producing assemblies that meet or exceed IPC J-STD-001 Class 3 acceptance criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Availability to work second shift on a consistent schedule, with willingness to work overtime or weekends to support critical production milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 25 lbs unassisted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range: California&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$96,760&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$137,352 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;line-height: 1;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Base salary will vary depending on job-related knowledge, education, skills, experience, business needs, and market demand. Salary is just one component of our comprehensive compensation package. Full-time employees also receive company equity, as well as access to a full suite of compelling benefits and perks, including: medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and dependents, generous paid time off; up to 20+ days of vacation for exempt staff and up to 10+ days of vacation for non-exempt staff with the ability to cash-out unused vacation annually, paid parental leave, short and long-term disability insurance, life insurance, access to a 401(k) retirement plan, ClassPass credits, personalized mental healthcare through Spring Health, and other discounts and perks. We also take pride in offering exceptional food perks, with snacks, drip coffee &amp;amp; onsite barista, cold drinks, and dinner meals remaining free of charge, and lunch subsidized as part of Vast’s ongoing commitment to providing high-quality meals for employees.&lt;/p&gt;
