&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Vast, our mission is to contribute to a future where billions of people are living and thriving in space. Vast is developing next-generation space stations to ensure a continuous human presence in space for America and its allies, enabling advanced microgravity research and manufacturing, and unlocking a new space economy for government, corporate, and private customers. Using an incremental, hardware-rich and low-cost approach, Vast is rapidly developing its multi-module Haven Station. Haven Demo’s 2025 success made Vast the only operational commercial space station company to fly and operate its own spacecraft. Next, Haven-1 is expected to become the world’s first commercial space station when it launches, followed by additional Haven modules to enable permanent human presence by 2030. Our team is all-in, committed to executing our mission safely and on time. If you want to work with the most talented people on Earth furthering space exploration for humanity, come join us.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vast is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Test&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Instrumentation Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, reporting to the&lt;strong&gt; Senior Manager, Engineering (E-2), &lt;/strong&gt;to support the development of the systems that will be required for the design, build, and test of the E-2 LOX/Kerosene oxidizer-rich staged combustion engine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This will be a full-time, &lt;strong&gt;exempt&lt;/strong&gt; position located at our &lt;strong&gt;Mojave Test Site&lt;/strong&gt; location.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role encompasses two core responsibilities: serving as a console operator during hazardous operations and owning the instrumentation, EGSE, and DAQ systems on the test stand.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as Test Conductor and Test Director during static fire testing of the E-2 engine, ensuring safe and disciplined execution of test operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, coordinate, and lead hazardous operations involving high-pressure systems, cryogenic fluids, and rocket propulsion hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and oversee test stand instrumentation and control systems across rocket engine and component test facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, update, and maintain electrical schematics for test stand instrumentation and control systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage instrumentation calibration records, ensuring traceability, accuracy, and compliance with required standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee calibration equipment inventory, usage, and maintenance, including coordination of recalibration activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with skilled technicians to design, build, test, maintain, and troubleshoot Electrical Ground Support Equipment (EGSE).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and resolve electrical, mechanical, and software-related issues on test stands to ensure operational readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement continuous improvements to enhance safety, reliability, and operational efficiency at the test site.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and participate in Test Readiness Reviews (TRRs), including verification of test objectives, procedures, and safety requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in an engineering discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience working with instrumentation and control systems in an operational, design, or development capacity, preferably in test stand or industrial environments.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with industrial sensors and instrumentation, including strain gauges, IEPE accelerometers, thermocouples (TCs), RTDs, and 4–20 mA current loop systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read, interpret, and work from technical documentation, including wiring diagrams, sensor datasheets, equipment manuals, and system schematics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret plumbing and instrumentation diagrams (P&amp;amp;IDs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with National Instruments (NI) hardware and LabVIEW-based data acquisition and control systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in programming and scripting languages such as Python, MATLAB, C/C++, SQL, and Git for version control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with high-pressure fluid and gas systems, including safe operation, monitoring, and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze operational or test data and implement corrective actions based on findings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Siemens NX and Teamcenter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Jira and Confluence for workflow tracking and technical documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail with a high level of accountability and ownership of work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with demonstrated ability to work effectively in team environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced, dynamic environment with rapidly changing priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to work overtime, or weekends to support critical mission milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility required as hours can vary depending on operational needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift up to 50 lbs unassisted and work in an outdoor, physically demanding test environment (from freezing conditions to temps up to 120 degrees fahrenheit)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
